A||N||3||Cozmo||2.8 chugs and sputters...(long)||||11||
Z||000000||Cozmo||05-03-2001||09:57 AM||||Perplexed...<BR>After a long and difficult process I finally got the 2.8 in the Targa reassembled.  Here's what was wrong when I got it:<BR>Leaky water pump and blown head gasket (I can see where these problems could go together...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<BR>I replaced the pump and redid the top end of the engine (reconditioned heads, cleaned up the intake stuff, ported exhausts, etc.)  This is the first time I've ever gotten this far into an engine and I was a little apprehensive to attempt this level of work.  With the encouragement of this forum and the help of some of my club members I decided to do the job myself.<BR>   Reassembly went fine, didn't have too many parts left over... stuck a battery in it, did a dance to the Fiero Gods then cranked it...<BR><B>Started right up!!!</B><BR>Did the Victory Dance then, hurt my arm patting myself on the back etc.  <BR>Set the timing, burped the coolant and generally watched it while I cycled it through a couple of temp. cycles.  All seemed fine, so time for a test drive.  It ran GREAT!! Idled at 1K, plenty of power, no funny noises, ran smooth.<BR>   Drove it about 80 miles then it started to get weird...<BR>at about 3K RPMs it would start to cut out, then started losing power and missing thru the whole RPM range.  I limped it back to the shop and started looking at it.  <BR>Mantra= Fuel, Air, Spark.  Looked like it was getting air. It is getting spark, but how good it is I don't know.  I have a couple of spare engines, started swapping the TPS, MAP, ign. module, dist. cap and rotor, plug wires (plugs are new AC Delco rapidfires gapped at .045"),  tach filter, coil, finally the whole distributor. No appreciable difference, in fact it ran progressively worse during this whole process. Then examined the fuel system, put a new filter on no joy.  Checked the Shrader valve for pressure, it's there but not a lot... S/B 45 PSI, when I press down the valve it fountains about 6" is that about right?  I'll probably get a pressure gauge and really measure it.<BR>   The only code I got was 13, TPS sensor I have 2 others from known good cars I tried no difference. The only thing I found funny was the O2 sensor was sheared off at the down pipe and the wire was dangling, didn't get a code on that, tho. Put one in no difference.<BR>   I'm leaning towards the fuel pump, will get a gauge this weekend and see if that's it. It really groans on startup and the car sat for about 3 years before I got it. <BR>Anybody got any other ideas or suggestions?  I've read the archives for hours on this, I learned a lot but obviously not enough to diagnose this problem...<BR>Help from the wizards, Pleez.....  <P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B><p>[This message has been edited by Cozmo (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||Wolfhound||05-03-2001||10:41 AM||||Code 13 is oxygen sensor! clear the codes by disconecting the battery and see if it sets new codes.<BR>Coy<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cozmo||05-03-2001||11:00 AM||||OOPS!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>I must have had a bad attack of the DUMBASS again...<BR>OK...I reset the codes when I installed the O2 sensor. Still the same symptoms.<BR>Did I break something by driving it approx. 80 mi. without an O2 sensor in the loop? If so, possibly what?<BR>I shure hope not...<BR>C02M0||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||05-04-2001||10:47 PM||||OK, I changed the fuel pump no difference.  Now it won't even stay running...Fires up normally than dies immediately. The pump stays running for about 2 seconds after the engine dies, than the lack of oil pressure shuts it off. Kinda discouraged now, I was afraid something like this would happen.  I'll tear into it again tomorrow and see if a new day brings any insights.  I would really appreciate any suggestions or input on how to track down this problem so I can start enjoying this cool car.<BR>Help! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>C02M0||||reg||5
